<speak>A label seems harmless enough. One drawer at a time also leaves the rest of the house usable, which is important when you're trying to spend more time there rather than create another ongoing task. You can stop after a small section and still feel you've finished something. The same idea works for your portal routine: one document session at a comfortable time, not a constant stream of checking. The administrative habits should support your day, not occupy every gap in it.</speak>